```java
// The whole feature, before:
double fee = isPremiumUser ? 0.0 : 2.99;

// After, "for extensibility":
interface FeeStrategy { double calculate(); }
class PremiumFee implements FeeStrategy { public double calculate() { return 0.0; } }
class StandardFee implements FeeStrategy { public double calculate() { return 2.99; } }
class FeeStrategyFactory {
    static FeeStrategy create(boolean isPremium) {
        return isPremium ? new PremiumFee() : new StandardFee();
    }
}
```

Four new types and a factory replaced one line, with no requirement that this ever grows past two cases — the "extensibility" being bought here was never asked for.
